WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:06.240
The Clone Wars-era Ahsoka Tano has finally made&nbsp;
her live-action debut — and you might have noticed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:11.280
she was played by a familiar face. So who is&nbsp;
Ariana Greenblatt, the actor who played her?

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:16.200
Like many young actors before her, Ariana&nbsp;
Greenblatt got her start working on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:20.760
small screen — and, before long, she became&nbsp;
one of the faces of the Disney Channel. After&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:25.260
playing a few minor roles in Disney shows,&nbsp;
Greenblatt's big break came courtesy of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:29.940
the sitcom Stuck in the Middle, which ran&nbsp;
for three seasons between 2016 and 2018.

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:34.560
Stuck in the Middle sees Greenblatt play&nbsp;
Daphne Diaz, the youngest sibling in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:38.100
family with six children. The character&nbsp;
is known for vandalizing her dolls,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:42.660
her unique sense of style, and her&nbsp;
precocious nature. Speaking to J-14,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:47.220
Greenblatt said that she imagines Daphne will&nbsp;
grow up to start her own business — and that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:51.240
it'll probably involve dolls. Spin-off?&nbsp;
It hasn't happened yet, but who knows?

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:54.900
While Stuck in the Middle boasts an&nbsp;
all-star cast — including a young Jenna&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:59.160
Ortega — Greenblatt's unique character&nbsp;
and impressive performance helped her to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:02.760
stand out from the pack. It seems she was&nbsp;
always destined for big things, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:07.440
and it didn't take long for the actress to get&nbsp;
offered movie roles after the Disney sitcom ended.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:12.060
Shortly after catching her big break&nbsp;
on the small screen, Ariana Greenblatt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:17.280
landed her first feature film role, starring&nbsp;
in the 2017 comedy A Bad Moms Christmas. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:21.900
sequel to 2016's Bad Moms follows a group&nbsp;
of overburdened mothers who are forced to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:25.620
contend with their own parents during the&nbsp;
holiday season. Hijinks ensue, of course.

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:28.080
In the movie, Greenblatt plays Lori Harkness,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:33.240
the daughter of Jay Hernandez and Mila Kunis'&nbsp;
characters. In one of the film's funniest scenes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:37.440
Lori confronts her mother about the strange&nbsp;
noises and foul language that she hears coming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:41.340
out of her parent's bedroom, which results&nbsp;
in an awkward exchange between the pair.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:45.780
In an interview with Bionic Buzz, Greenblatt&nbsp;
said that she loved working with her co-stars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:49.290
adding that collaborating with them was&nbsp;
the highlight of the entire shoot. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:52.680
while A Bad Moms Christmas gave her the&nbsp;
chance to show off her comedic chops,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:56.100
Greenblatt was about to make a big&nbsp;
leap into a very different franchise…

00:01:57.060 --> 00:01:59.500
"What did it cost you?"

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:03.863
"Everything."

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:08.160
Ariana Greenblatt's outing as the young&nbsp;
Jedi Ahsoka Tano isn't the first time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:11.520
that she's played a younger version of&nbsp;
a formidable hero in a hugely popular&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:15.660
franchise. Prior to starring on Ahsoka,&nbsp;
she portrayed young Gamora in Avengers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:19.560
Infinity War, featuring in a pair of&nbsp;
scenes alongside Josh Brolin's Thanos.

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:23.700
Greenblatt's big moment occurs when Thanos and&nbsp;
his forces invade the young Gamora's home planet.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:28.440
Despite her best efforts to fight off some of the&nbsp;
villain's minions, she can't resist his offer of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:33.480
help. Thus begins a dysfunctional father-daughter&nbsp;
relationship that, ultimately, ends in tragedy.

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:35.880
Most actors would do anything to be part of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:39.120
Star Wars and Marvel franchises.&nbsp;
And it seems that Greenblatt can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:43.080
now tick both off her list — despite the&nbsp;
fact her career is just getting started.

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:47.640
Based on Katherine Alice Applegate's&nbsp;
novel of the same name, The One and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:51.060
Only Ivan tells the story of a gorilla&nbsp;
who teams up with an elephant to escape&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:55.620
from captivity. Ariana Greenblatt plays&nbsp;
Julia, an artistically driven child who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:58.500
develops a bond with the ape through&nbsp;
their shared sense of loneliness.

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:02.760
This role struck a chord with the young actress&nbsp;
at the time. During a conversation with the Movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:07.620
Times, Greenblatt explained that she was already&nbsp;
a fan of the book prior to landing the part. In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:11.460
the same interview, Greenblatt also opened up&nbsp;
about what attracted her to the role of Julia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:15.660
in the first place. According to the actress,&nbsp;
she identified with the character due to their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:19.080
mutual love of animals and drawing —&nbsp;
making it quite the fun role to play.

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:25.200
In 2020, Ariana Greenblatt landed a supporting&nbsp;
role in Netflix's post-apocalyptic creature&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:30.060
flick Love and Monsters. The story centers around&nbsp;
Joel Dawson and his loyal canine friend as they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:34.380
embark on an adventure to reunite with Joel's high&nbsp;
school sweetheart. This adventure brings them into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:39.360
contact with a cast of fascinating characters,&nbsp;
including Greenblatt's survivalist expert, Minnow.

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:43.680
One of the film's standout characters, Minnow&nbsp;
accompanies Michael Rooker's character, Clyde,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:46.920
in his quest to find a safe haven in&nbsp;
the harsh wastelands. They're both&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:49.260
portrayed as experts at surviving in the ravaged&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:52.980
new world and work together to overcome&nbsp;
the monstrous threats that dwell there.

00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:57.000
"What you so scared for?&nbsp;
The older snails are nice."

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:58.380
"There can be nice ones?"

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:03.180
This is arguably one of Greenblatt's most mature&nbsp;
roles to date, as her character is one who has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:07.320
experienced some tough times during her short&nbsp;
life. She also capably holds her own alongside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:12.360
veteran actor Rooker, making their characters&nbsp;
feel more like equals than an adult-child pairing.

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:17.820
Awake tells the story of a catastrophic event&nbsp;
that simultaneously takes away humankind's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:21.780
ability to fall asleep and shuts off all of the&nbsp;
world's electronics. With the world trapped in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:26.220
a state of insomnia-induced hysteria and no&nbsp;
means to recharge, people gradually become&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:30.960
more and more unhinged, forcing scientists to&nbsp;
come up with a solution before time runs out.

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:35.820
Ariana Greenblatt plays Matilda in Awake, a child&nbsp;
who, as one of the few who is able to sleep,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:40.560
might hold the key to humankind's salvation.&nbsp;
However, this puts her in considerable danger,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:44.640
as some people want to sacrifice her;&nbsp;
meanwhile, Matilda's mother wants to keep&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:48.360
her alive at all costs and come up with&nbsp;
an alternative solution to the problem.

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:52.620
While Awake didn't exactly receive heaps of&nbsp;
critical acclaim, Greenblatt's performance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:57.180
certainly caught Hollywood's attention, as she&nbsp;
moved on to a number of other noteworthy projects&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.180 --> 00:05:01.440
afterward. And the actress credits this one as&nbsp;
one of her favorite roles, telling Unpublished&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:05.580
Zine that it allowed her to showcase more acting&nbsp;
range than ever before at the time. She said:

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:09.180
"This role really pushed me and shows&nbsp;
an emotional range and it is very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:12.720
action-packed which is something I've&nbsp;
never done before. It was so much fun."

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:18.060
An adaptation of Lin-Manuel Miranda's first hit&nbsp;
stage musical, In the Heights hit theaters in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:23.040
2021. The film follows Usnavi, a New York City&nbsp;
bodega owner who dreams about living a better&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:27.060
life. He wants to go back to his native&nbsp;
Dominican Republic, so he saves up his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:31.080
pennies in the hope of realizing that ambition.&nbsp;
Greenblatt plays the younger version of Nina,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:35.040
a lead character who returns home from college&nbsp;
to spend the summer in the neighborhood.

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:39.000
The musical genre turned out to be a good fit&nbsp;
for Greenblatt. While she doesn't have one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:43.020
the main roles in In The Heights, her history&nbsp;
as a dancer makes her perfect for roles of this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.020 --> 00:05:47.400
ilk. During a conversation with Elle, she said&nbsp;
that she's been dancing for most of her life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:51.360
so it wouldn't be surprising if she tackles&nbsp;
more roles in this genre down the line. In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:54.660
the meantime, fans who want to check out&nbsp;
Greenblatt's skills can also revisit her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:58.560
tenure on Dancing with the Stars, where&nbsp;
she finished as a fourth-placed runner-up.

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:06.060
"I'm feeling so excited, a little nervous, but&nbsp;
I'm very ready to meet my partner. Let's go!"

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:09.780
Ariana Greenblatt has apparently developed&nbsp;
something of a taste for post-apocalyptic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:13.080
movies. But while most of them have&nbsp;
been sci-fi stories set in the future,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:16.680
one of her most recent roles is&nbsp;
set 65 billion years in the past.

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:22.020
In 65, the actress plays Koa, a survivor of a&nbsp;
catastrophic event who must team up with Adam&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:26.760
Driver's Mills to survive a land of dinosaurs.&nbsp;
Cue an adventure that's reminiscent of The Last&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:30.600
of Us with elements of Jurassic Park and&nbsp;
A Quiet Place thrown in for good measure.

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:36.000
Some critics lambasted 65 as a dino-bore that&nbsp;
failed to live up to its intriguing premise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:40.140
but Greenblatt worked well with the material&nbsp;
and further proved that she's a rising star&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.140 --> 00:06:44.220
in the world of sci-fi and horror. Notably,&nbsp;
this was arguably her biggest role to date,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:47.940
as it placed her front and center as&nbsp;
a co-lead in a big budget blockbuster.

00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:54.660
65 might not go down in history as one of 2023's&nbsp;
most acclaimed movies, but Barbie is arguably a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.660 --> 00:06:58.800
generation-defining blockbuster. In addition to&nbsp;
being one of this year's most successful movies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:03.420
both commercially and critically, Greta Gerwig's&nbsp;
hit proved that auteur visions can appeal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:07.800
to mainstream audiences. Ariana Greenblatt&nbsp;
plays a standout part in the movie as Sasha,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:11.820
an angsty Gen Z teen who lost interest&nbsp;
in playing with dolls a long time ago.

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:15.180
Sasha is one of the main human&nbsp;
characters in Barbie. The titular&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:18.240
doll comes to the human world&nbsp;
to find Sasha's mother, Gloria,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:22.500
a disgruntled Mattel employee who's trying to&nbsp;
find her purpose in life. Initially, though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:26.520
Barbie thinks she's coming to help the teen.&nbsp;
Sasha and Gloria don't always see eye-to-eye,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:30.780
and their relationship is at the heart of some&nbsp;
of the film's funniest and most dramatic scenes.

00:07:30.780 --> 00:07:35.160
"Are you really going to let Barbie take you&nbsp;
and your tween daughter to an imaginary land?"

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:37.260
"Yes, and you wanna know why?&nbsp;
Because I never get to do anything."

00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:40.680
For Greenblatt, portraying the Gen&nbsp;
Z'er was an opportunity for her to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:43.800
play an authentic teenage girl on the&nbsp;
screen. She told the Hollywood Reporter:

00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:48.300
"I tried to at least make [Sasha] as relatable&nbsp;
as possible. I wanted to represent teenage girls&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:52.440
appropriately. No one understands a teenage&nbsp;
girl unless you were one once in your life."

00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:56.820
Ariana Greenblatt's next feature film role&nbsp;
will see her return to familiar ground,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.820 --> 00:08:01.860
as she's set to play Tiny Tina in Eli Roth's&nbsp;
upcoming Borderlands adaptation. The sci-fi&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.860 --> 00:08:05.700
actioner will chronicle the adventures of&nbsp;
a band of misfits as they travel across an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:09.780
alien-infested planet to find the daughter&nbsp;
of one of the most important people in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:13.620
universe. In addition to aliens, the heroes&nbsp;
will also have to contend with bandits,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.620 --> 00:08:16.740
savages, and the other villainous&nbsp;
deviants who populate the planet.

00:08:16.740 --> 00:08:21.540
It remains to be seen how each character will be&nbsp;
portrayed in the movie, but Tina, Greenblatt's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.540 --> 00:08:25.800
character, has been described as "feral." Indeed,&nbsp;
this might be her most unhinged role to date,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.800 --> 00:08:30.000
and it's bound to showcase a whole new side&nbsp;
of her acting sensibilities. Furthermore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:33.360
with Roth at the helm, coupled with the&nbsp;
source material that inspired the movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:37.320
this is bound to be a violent affair with&nbsp;
plenty of dark humor thrown into the mix.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:41.340
For Borderlands, Greenblatt will be joined by&nbsp;
an all-star cast that includes Cate Blanchett,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.340 --> 00:08:44.880
Jack Black, Jamie Lee Curtis,&nbsp;
Kevin Hart, and many more.

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:49.320
Unfortunately, Borderlands won't be released&nbsp;
until next August. Following Ahsoka, though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:54.240
it's only a matter of time until Ariana Greenblatt&nbsp;
appears in even more high-profile projects.

